  "body": "### Description\n\nBy only mistyping “confirm password” once, a user ID is taken despite an error return “Password do not match”.\r\n\r\nAfter restarting a server it returned an error “Error during initialisation: database is locked”\r\nSecond start, “started synapse.app.homeserver”\r\nThe user ID with the mismatched password returns,\r\n“Sending registration request...\r\nERROR! Received 400 Bad Request\r\nUser ID already taken.”\r\n\r\nIs there a way to delete such a user-ID to reuse it again?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nregister_new_matrix_user -c homeserver.yaml\r\nEnter  a user Name/ID\r\nPassword \"Right\"\r\nConfirm Password \"Wrong\"\r\n\r\nsynctl restart\r\n\r\nError during initialisation:\r\ndatabase is locked\r\n\r\n\n\n### Homeserver\n\nmy own homeserver\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n1.63.1\n\n### Installation Method\n\nDebian packages from packages.matrix.org\n\n### Platform\n\nProxmox - Container - Ubuntu 22.04 - python_version:\"3.10.4\"\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nNew user localpart [root]: joe\r\nPassword: \r\nConfirm password: \r\nMake admin [no]: yes\r\nSending registration request...\r\nERROR! Received 400 Bad Request\r\nUser ID already taken.\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\n_No response_",
